/* Twins programming language, by Wellyton B. Galdino 

    Twins is a statically typed programming language, that is 
    designed to help programmers to write Web applications with
    a full compilation process that is so helpfull in other languages.

    Twins takes inspirations by C, Elixir, Lua, Python and glues everything
    togheter to give programmers a good experience while programming web
    interfaces.

    I want to make this a fully functional programming language for the Web
    I don't know how far this will go, but let's see it.
*/

/* FUNCTIONS
    functions can be declared wit a notation similar to python and c
    type name(args...): 
        ...
    end
    since a function is not a tag, dont need : in end keyword
*/

int count():
	value = value + 1
end

int state value = 0

/* TAGS AND PAGES
    To use a HTML tag, you can use ":" followed by the name of the tag
    everithing you write in : will be translated to a tag.

    To create a function that returns a page content or a component, you
    need to specify the view type, and then, you can write tags normally.
*/

view DummyExample()
    :html
	    :head
		    :title <Dumb Example>
	    :end

	    :body
		    :button onclick={count} 
                Click me idiot ${value}
            :end
            :p <<This is a page written in Twins>>
            :a href="https://wellyxs.com/twins" <<Twins docs>>
	    :end
    :end
end
